'''Ultra Greed Coins''' are enemies exclusively spawned by {{e|Ultra Greed}} during some of his attacks.

=== Spinner Coin ===
{{infobox monster
 | dlc         = a
 | name        = Ultra Greed Coin (Spinner)
 | id          = 293
 | base hp     = 50
 | environment = {{floor|Ultra Greed}}
 | behavior    = Spins around the room, dealing contact damage.
}}

'''Spinner Coins''' will spin around the room. Unlike the other coins, these deal contact damage, but won't do anything if they are not destroyed in time. They also last longer.
{{clear}}

=== Key Coin ===
{{infobox monster
 | dlc         = a
 | name        = Ultra Greed Coin (Key)
 | variant     = 1
 | base hp     = 60
 | environment = {{floor|Ultra Greed}}
 | behavior    = Spins on itself and opens a golden door around the room if not destroyed, spawning hordes of [[Greed Gaper]]s.
}}

'''Key Coins''' open the golden doors around Ultra Greed's boss room if not destroyed, which spawn hordes of {{e|Greed Gaper}}s.
{{clear}}

=== Bomb Coin ===
{{infobox monster
 | dlc         = a
 | name        = Ultra Greed Coin (Bomb)
 | variant     = 2
 | base hp     = 50
 | environment = {{floor|Ultra Greed}}
 | behavior    = Spins on itself and explodes with a large radius if not destroyed.
}}

'''Bomb Coins''' explode with a large radius if not destroyed, but a single explosion can deal 40 damage to Ultra Greed. Bomb Coins spawned by {{e|Ultra Greedier}} can drop a {{e|Penny}}.
{{clear}}

=== Heart Coin ===
{{infobox monster
 | dlc         = a
 | name        = Ultra Greed Coin (Heart)
 | variant     = 3
 | base hp     = 40
 | environment = {{floor|Ultra Greed}}
 | behavior    = Spins on itself and heals Ultra Greed for 13.125 HP each if not destroyed.
}}

'''Heart Coins''' heal Ultra Greed for 13.125 HP each if not destroyed.
{{clear}}

== Notes ==
* The Coins all gain +15% HP after unlocking {{a|Everything is Terrible 2!!!}} and their timings (breaking up and activating effect) are 10% faster.

